# Rust engine migration workflow

## Architecture (locked — do not forget)

**Engine works. UI shows.**

| Rust engine | NOT engine (UI only) |
|-------------|----------------------|
| `packages/api`, `packages/storage`, `packages/core` models | Widgets, nav, player chrome |
| `packages/scrapers`, `webstreamr`, `streaming` | WebView **host** |
| HTTP, storage, parse, torrent, proxy | |

All left-column packages **move to `crates/`** in Phase 2. Phase 3 does **not** port them to Kotlin.

## Before coding

1. Read [docs/migration/README.md](../../docs/migration/README.md).
2. Active: [02-rust-engine-complete.md](../../docs/migration/02-rust-engine-complete.md).
3. **Do not start Phase 3** until P2-82–89 + P2-86 done.

## Wire-up pattern

- **Target:** UI calls `ForjaEngine.searchTorrents()` / uniffi — one FFI call per user action.
- **Legacy (delete in P2-86):** `*Backend` hooks, `rust_delegates.dart`.
- **Never** call engine from `compute()` isolates.

## After engine work

1. Update [02-rust-engine-complete.md](../../docs/migration/02-rust-engine-complete.md).
2. Run `./scripts/build_rust.sh`, `cargo test --workspace`, `cd packages/rust && flutter test`.

## Doc status rules

- `packages/api` and `packages/storage` are **engine**, not UI-adjacent.
- Phase 3 = UI swap only.
